IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sk73-nouns`
IMPORT `sk73-cross-references`

-- Row il-73. TESTS OF THE CONTROLS: the sound references kept beside the two defects. They pass.
-- Each control tests that a thing exists where the row says it is, so that a failing item is not a failure of the test itself.
-- The expected values are hand-written from the quotation lines in sk73-cross-references.l4 and from the printed pages, not copied from the values there.

§ `Tests of the controls for item I1`

-- SH 2203 section 132 prints (b)(2) with both enactment names: the test finds the names when they are there.
#ASSERT `the provision prints the name of the enactment` `SH 2203 section 4A(b)(2) as printed` `the Bankruptcy Ordinance as section 4A(b)(2) names it`
#ASSERT `the provision prints the name of the enactment` `SH 2203 section 4A(b)(2) as printed` `the Companies Ordinance as section 4A(b)(2) names it`

-- SH 2459 Schedule item 21 names the Law without an exception, and pair (11) replaces a word of (b)(2): the 2014 law reached (b)(2) and changed that word.
#ASSERT `SH 2459 Schedule item 21`'s `the item number` EQUALS 21
#ASSERT NOT (`SH 2459 Schedule item 21`'s `an exception is printed with the item`)
#ASSERT `the replaced word is a token of the provision` `pair (11) of SH 2459 section 1` `SH 2203 section 4A(b)(2) as printed`

-- Pair (11) is not the name of either enactment, and no pair of section 1 of SH 2459 contains either name.
#ASSERT NOT (`the replaced word is the name of the enactment` `pair (11) of SH 2459 section 1` `the Bankruptcy Ordinance as section 4A(b)(2) names it`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the replaced word is the name of the enactment` `pair (11) of SH 2459 section 1` `the Companies Ordinance as section 4A(b)(2) names it`)
#ASSERT `the pairs of SH 2459 section 1 searched for the two names`'s `the number of pairs that contain the name of either enactment` EQUALS 0

-- The phrase of (b)(2) for a winding-up order is printed on both sides: in section 342G(a) as inserted by SH 2708 section 360(10), and in section 266 of the 1983 print.
#ASSERT `the provision prints the token` `SH 2203 section 4A(b)(2) as printed` "צו פירוק"
#ASSERT `the provision prints the token` `SH 2708 section 342G(a) as printed` "צו פירוק"
#ASSERT `the provision prints the token` `DMI 37 section 266` "צו פירוק"

-- The instrument that adds section 4A and the instrument that repeals are two different issues.
#ASSERT `the two issues are different` (`SH 2203 section 132`'s `the issue`) (`SH 2708 section 358`'s `the issue`)

§ `Tests of the controls for item I2`

-- SH 856 adds chapter ג׳2 in section 3 and, in the same instrument, section 10 cites it: the cited chapter is added by the instrument that cites it.
#ASSERT `the two instructions are in one issue` `SH 856 section 3` `SH 856 section 10`
#ASSERT `the instruction that added the chapter gives it the number the citing words write` `item I2: section 11 cites chapter ג׳2 of the National Insurance Law`

-- The title of chapter ו׳ of the 1995 print equals the title SH 856 gave chapter ג׳2.
#ASSERT `the two titles are the same words` `item I2: section 11 cites chapter ג׳2 of the National Insurance Law`

-- The margin bracket of chapter ו׳ and the table row agree on ג׳2: two printed places, one answer.
#ASSERT `the bracket and the table row agree on the number the citing words write` `item I2: section 11 cites chapter ג׳2 of the National Insurance Law`

-- The string section 10 replaces occurs in section 11 as SH 814 prints it: the test finds the string when it is there.
#ASSERT `the string replaced is a token of the provision` `the string replacement of SH 856 section 10` `SH 814 section 11 as printed`

-- The instrument that cites the chapter and the 1995 print are two different issues.
#ASSERT `the two issues are different` (`SH 856 section 10`'s `the issue`) `issue SH 1522`
